title: Subagent depth limit should error gracefully without killing parent
updated_at: "2026-08-02T11:37:11Z"
---
When a subagent at max depth tries to spawn another subagent, it should get a clean error response instead of failing hard. The depth check should only trigger in that specific circumstance (prohibited nesting) and must not kill or disrupt any parent subagent(s) in the chain.